# Creative Suite design language

Source of truth: Figma **Creative Suite** (`mH4MAAEe27RAt2W7jo8Aio`), from redesigned ADA frame `62:2`, implemented at **0.5×** of the Figma artboard. Match this language — not IBM Plex Mono / black composite rules, and not Are.na.

## Tokens (`assets/design.css`)

| Role | Value |
|------|--------|
| Background | `#FFFFFF` |
| Active / primary text | `#333333` (`--ink`) |
| Labels / inactive | `#696969` (`--muted`) |
| Borders / tracks / hairlines | `#EDEDED` |
| Chip / track fill | `#EDEDED` (`--surface`) |
| Rail thumb | `#696969` (`--thumb`) |
| Box radius | `2.5px` (Figma 5 × 0.5) |
| Rail radius | `3.75px` (Figma 7.5 × 0.5) |
| Box border | `1px solid #EDEDED` (Figma 2 × 0.5) |
| Typeface | **Inter only** (400 labels / 600 active) |
| Type size (suite) | **`15px`** (`--suite-fs`) — header, home, Multi-export, Logo-variant, Color-check, Mesh-gradient, and new UI unless stated otherwise |
| Type size (legacy tool chrome) | **`12.5px`** (`--fs`) — Figma 25 × 0.5 on older tool panels until redesigned |

## Hard rules

- **Suite type default**: Inter **15px** (`--suite-fs`), tracking `-1px` where the menu/Multi-export language applies. Use this for header, home, Multi-export, Logo-variant, Color-check, Mesh-gradient, and new suite screens unless a design states otherwise.
- **Legacy tool chrome**: older tools still use `var(--fs)` / `12.5px` for panel UI until redesigned.
- **Inter by default**: no monospace UI chrome; `--mono` aliases to Inter. Chart-font overrides are opt-in only.
- **Rail selectors**: `--rail-w: 7.5px` track + thumb; active `#333` semibold, inactive `#696969`.
- **Chips**: `--chip-h: 22.5px`, soft `#EDEDED`, `2.5px` radius.
- **Sentence case** labels (`Standard`, `Show only`).
- **Menu**: horizontal bar (Figma `91:3` / `91:58`). Inter **15px** (`--suite-fs`), tracking `-1px`, ink `#000`, muted `#969696`. Tools hover expands so Information + clock slide right. Tool hover → `#000`. Click → bar rises; Information is coming soon (still `#000`).
- **Suite grid**: **5 columns** (margin `20px`, gutter `21px`). Tool rows: menu track `1fr` (bar at top → vertical gap) · controls `auto` · drop `1fr×3`. Home: same columns, bar vertically centered.
- **Tools**: Color-check → ADA · Multi-export → Export · Mesh-gradient → Brandboard · Logo-variant → Varlogo · Color-swap → Recolor.
- When reading new Figma: honor the frame’s layout grid; menu/home/suite screens default to **15px** unless the frame specifies otherwise.

## Adaptation workflow

1. `get_design_context` on the Figma node (design-to-code skill).
2. Map into `.box`, `.rail-*`, `.stat-row`, `.chip`, `.opt` in `design.css`.
3. Scale Figma px × 0.5; default suite type to `--suite-fs` (15px); legacy tool chrome may still use `--fs` (12.5px) until redesigned.
4. Extend tokens/rule if a new pattern appears — don’t fork a one-off look.
5. Avoid naming collisions with shell classes (`.panel` is the left nav — use a scoped name for tool-local panels).
